A52 — release limited frames on a time grid, snapped to the panel's latch grid

The non-VRR frame-rate limit counted compositor wakeups: a window got its frame
callback on every (refresh / target)th wakeup, which equals every Nth vblank only
while no wakeup is ever late. The timer re-arms by stepping to the next vblank
after "now", so a wakeup that comes more than one vblank late skips the vblanks
in between, and those never count. On the 1200 Hz grid a session runs on, a
wakeup is late by a vblank after 0.83 ms of scheduling delay, and every late one
holds the next frame a whole vblank longer: the cap reads below the target in
proportion to the wakeups lost, and sinks further as the device throttles.

The limiter now keeps a release grid in time: the next release is the previous
one plus the target period, and a frame is released on the first vblank whose
nominal time reaches it, with half a vblank of tolerance for the anchor moving.
A late wakeup delays that one release by the lateness, and the grid absorbs it
on the next, so the average rate is the target. A stall longer than a period is
a lost frame, never a debt to repay with back-to-back releases.

That grid is still free-running against the panel. The daemon stamps the flip
events on its own 1200 Hz timeline, so nothing ties a release to where
SurfaceFlinger latches, and with a 60 cap on a 60 Hz panel the commits drift
across the latch deadline: two land on one latch point and one is replaced,
measured as 59.4 commits/s shown at 56.7 fps, where at 120 Hz (every commit
its own latch point) the same session shows all 59.4. So when the DRM shim
answers the panel's latch grid (gamenative_drm_latch_grid, weak: anchor, period,
lead, measured by the daemon from the latch stats) and the target period is a
whole number of latch periods, the release grid is snapped onto the latch grid,
offset by a lead the limiter steers itself: each commit's time is read against
the grid, and the lead moves an eighth of the error toward landing commits in
the middle of their latch window, so none sits on the edge and no two share a
point. Without the symbol, or with a target the panel period does not divide,
the release grid stays free-running. The VRR path is untouched: it already
schedules by time.

